-- title:
--   Unit fundamental lemma at unramified v, prime degree
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $L$ be number fields with $L$ a $K$-algebra, assume the degree $\operatorname{finrank}_K L$ is a prime number, let $\sigma$ be a $K$-algebra automorphism of $L$ with $\sigma \neq 1$, and let $v$ be a height-one prime of $\mathcal{O}_K$ such that every height-one prime $w$ of $\mathcal{O}_L$ lying under-equal to $v$ (i.e. with $\mathrm{under}\,(\mathcal{O}_K)\,w = v$) has ramification index $1$ over $v$. The conclusion is the predicate `AreMatchingLocal` for the pair consisting of the $\mathbb{C}$-valued indicator function, with value $1$, of `semiLocalIntegralSet K L v` — the set of $g \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K K_v)$ such that both $g$ and $g^{-1}$ have all entries in the image of `HeightOneSpectrum.tensorAdicCompletionIntegersTo K L (𝓞 L) v` — and the indicator function, with value $1$, of `localIntegralSet K v`, the set of $g \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_v)$ with $g$ and $g^{-1}$ having entries in $\mathcal{O}_{K_v}$. Unfolded, this asserts `AreMatchingOn` for these two functions with respect to the Haar measures `semiLocalHaar K L v` and `localHaar K v` normalised on the corresponding compact sets of integral points: first, for every $\delta \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K K_v)$ whose $\sigma$-norm string `normString` is regular semisimple, every regular semisimple $\gamma \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_v)$, every $y$ exhibiting $\gamma$ as $\sigma$-norm of $\delta$ via `IsNormConjugator`, and all Haar measures $\tau$ on the centraliser of $\gamma$ and $\tau'$ on the $\sigma$-twisted centraliser of $\delta$ that are `Coupled` through $y$, any value $I'$ of the twisted orbital integral of the first function at $\delta$ for $\tau'$ equals any value $I$ of the orbital integral of the second at $\gamma$ for $\tau$; and second, for every regular semisimple $\gamma$ that is not a $\sigma$-norm of any $\delta$, every orbital integral value $I$ of the second function at $\gamma$, for any Haar measure on the centraliser of $\gamma$, vanishes.
--
--   This is the unit fundamental lemma for the $\sigma$-twisted comparison on $\mathrm{GL}_2$ at a finite place $v$ unramified in $L/K$, in the form needed for extensions of prime degree (where $\sigma \neq 1$ forces $L/K$ to be cyclic generated by $\sigma$): the unit of the local Hecke algebra is matched with the unit, covering both the split and the inert behaviour of $v$ in $L$. It feeds the trace comparisons used to transfer cuspidal data along base change, being cited in the identification of winding and hyperbolic-slope identities and in the non-vanishing criterion for the twisted cut trace on principal level.
